==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|ang|oferhangan}}, corresponding to {{prefix|en|over|hang}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əʊvəˈhaŋ/|a=UK}} (verb), {{IPA|en|/ˈəʊvəhaŋ/}} (noun)
* {{IPA|en|/ˈoʊvəɹˌhæŋ/|a=US}} (noun)
* {{audio|en|en-us-overhang.ogg|a=US}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|overhangs|overhanging|overhung|past2=overhanged}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[hang]] over (something).
#* {{RQ:Byron Don Juan|II|116|passage=Her brow was '''overhung''' with coins of gold, / That sparkled o'er the auburn of her hair [...].}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012  |title=Freedom...At Last! |author=Edwin Labre; Solly Border |page=37 |ISBN=|passage=At that time, the upper part of the tower '''overhanged''' its base by about fourteen feet.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[impend]].

